# Ways to pay a renewal down faster. Example
# inputs, with the posted 5 year rate from the
# Bank of Canada.

mortgage "Monthly"
  balance $380,000
  rate posted 5 year on 2026-11-18 fixed
  amortization 22 years
  term 5 years

scenario "Accelerated biweekly"
  payments accelerated biweekly

scenario "Extra $250 a month"
  extra $250 per payment

scenario "Lump sum each year"
  lump $6,000 every year

compare all by payment, yearly, interest, balance, payoff
show yearly "Lump sum each year"
show interest of "Monthly" - interest of "Lump sum each year"

# Three months of interest at the contract rate
# on the balance at the end of the term. This is
# a planning figure. Many contracts set their
# own prepayment charge. The Interest Act,
# s. 10 (1), gives a three months interest right
# only where the mortgage money is not payable
# until more than five years after the mortgage
# date, only after those five years, and
# s. 10 (2) leaves out mortgages given by a
# joint stock company or other corporation. This
# 5 year term is not long enough for s. 10 to
# apply.
show three months interest of "Monthly"
